<title>GERMANY: German trade seeks intvn rye, barley exports -BLE.</title>
<headline>German trade seeks intvn rye, barley exports -BLE.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders made bids for the export of 221,000 tonnes of intervention barley and 189,900 tonnes of intervention rye at this week's EU grain tender, state grain intervention board BLE said.</p>
<p>A BLE source said both volumes, for the export to third countries, included multiple bids for identical lots.</p>
<p>In barley, a maximum of 52,500 tonnes are left for export and in rye, the remainder is 151,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
